#: patterns/une-archipel.php:167
msgid ""
"L’histoire d’un manuscrit caché, recopié, sorti d’URSS, épisode par épisode."
msgstr ""
"The story of a manuscript hidden, copied and smuggled out of the USSR, "
"episode by episode."

#: patterns/une-archipel.php:179
msgid ""
"Le livre de Soljenitsyne sur les camps soviétiques paraît d’abord en russe, "
"à Paris, chez YMCA-Press, avant de faire le tour du monde."
msgstr ""
"Solzhenitsyn’s book on the Soviet camps first came out in Russian, in Paris,"
" from YMCA-Press, before going round the world."

#: patterns/une-archipel.php:183
msgid "Soljenitsyne et Nikita Struve à l’imprimerie"
msgstr "Solzhenitsyn and Nikita Struve at the printing works"

#: patterns/une-archipel.php:183
msgid ""
"Soljenitsyne, Nikita Struve, Léonide Lifar et Serge Béresniak. Photo Hélène "
"Lifar."
msgstr ""
"Solzhenitsyn, Nikita Struve, Léonide Lifar and Serge Béresniak. Photo: "
"Hélène Lifar."

#: patterns/une-archipel.php:189
msgid ""
"Soljenitsyne l’écrit en secret, entre 1958 et 1968, à partir de ses années "
"de camp et de plus de deux cents témoignages d’anciens détenus. Il le sous-"
"titre «&nbsp;essai d’investigation littéraire&nbsp;»&nbsp;: ni roman ni "
"livre d’histoire, mais les deux à la fois."
msgstr ""
"Solzhenitsyn wrote it in secret between 1958 and 1968, drawing on his years "
"in the camps and on more than two hundred accounts by former prisoners. He "
"subtitled it “an experiment in literary investigation”: neither a novel nor "
"a history book, but both at once."

#: patterns/une-archipel.php:193
msgid ""
"En 1973, le KGB saisit l’un des exemplaires du manuscrit&nbsp;; l’auteur "
"décide de le faire publier sans attendre. Le premier tome paraît à Paris le "
"28 décembre. En février 1974, Soljenitsyne est arrêté, déchu de sa "
"citoyenneté et expulsé d’URSS."
msgstr ""
"In 1973 the KGB seized one of the copies of the manuscript; the author "
"decided to have it published at once. The first volume came out in Paris on "
"28 December. In February 1974 Solzhenitsyn was arrested, stripped of his "
"citizenship and expelled from the USSR."

#: patterns/une-archipel.php:197
msgid ""
"Cinquante ans après, le recueil dirigé par Georges Nivat, <em>L’Archipel du "
"Goulag, cinquante ans après</em>, en reprend les pages essentielles, avec "
"les lectures qu’on en a faites depuis. Au centre culturel, un podcast en "
"plusieurs épisodes, <em>Les secrets de L’Archipel du Goulag</em>, raconte "
"les mystères d’un livre hors du commun."
msgstr ""
"Fifty years on, the collection edited by Georges Nivat, <em>L’Archipel du "
"Goulag, cinquante ans après</em>, brings together its essential pages and "
"the readings it has had since. At the cultural centre, a podcast in several "
"episodes, <em>The Secrets of The Gulag Archipelago</em>, tells the mysteries"
" of an extraordinary book."

